  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry orange. Using a vegetable peeler, remove one strip of orange zest for garnish. Juice orange into a small bowl, then measure out a 1/4 fl oz (1/2 tbsp) juice and add to a mixing glass. (Reserve remaining orange juice for another use.)",
      "secondary_message": "½ orange"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add 1 1/2 fl oz (3 tbsp) mezcal, 1/2 fl oz (1 tbsp) tequila, agave nectar, and bitters to the mixing glass. Stir until agave nectar is dissolved. ",
      "secondary_message": "44 ml Mezcal\n15 ml tequila\n½ tsp agave nectar\n⅛ tsp bitters"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add ice to the mixing glass. Stir until ice starts to melt and outside of glass is very cold, about 1 minute. ",
      "secondary_message": "⅔ cup ice cube"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place additional ice in an old fashioned glass or tumbler of choice. Strain cocktail over ice, then garnish with orange peel and a cherry. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": "⅓ cup ice cube\n1 maraschino cherry"
    }
  ],
